# Implementation Workflow Manager

## Default Entry Point: Phase Orchestrator

**Do not ask the user which agent to run.** Use the automatic pipeline.

| User says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| `start phase N` | Run [phase-orchestrator](../agents/phase-orchestrator/agent.md) for phase N |
| `next` / `continue` | Run orchestrator for next unchecked phase (see checklist below) |
| `merge` / `merge pr` | Merge open phase PR only when user explicitly requests |
| `status` | Report phase checklist and open PRs |

Full user guide: [`WORKFLOW.md`](../../WORKFLOW.md) at repo root.

## Mandatory Agent Chain (per phase)

The orchestrator runs this sequence **automatically** ? not optional:

```
1. Branch from main          phase-{N}-{description}
2. Implement                 generalPurpose + langgraph-bug-triage skill
3. @spec-architect           IF spec.md changed; else skip
4. @code-auditor             ALWAYS ? audit vs spec.md
   ?? critical ? @bug-fixer ? re-audit (max 2 loops)
5. @qa-tester                ALWAYS before PR
   Phase 1: environment only | Phase 2+: full Set B + edge cases
   ?? fail ? @bug-fixer ? re-test (max 3 loops)
6. Commit + push branch
7. gh pr create              template with audit + QA results
8. Report PR URL             DO NOT merge unless user says "merge"
```

**Never** skip code-auditor or qa-tester. **Never** merge without explicit user approval.

