## Purpose

Coordinates multi-phase implementation with proper Git workflow:

- Auto-creates feature branches for each phase
- Runs mandatory audit + QA agent chain
- Commits work to branch
- Creates PR with agent vs manual documentation
- Fix loops via bug-fixer when audit or QA fails

## When to Use

Apply when starting any implementation phase (2, 3, 4). Invoke **phase-orchestrator** ? not individual agents in isolation.

---

## Workflow Steps (orchestrator executes)

### 1. Branch Creation

```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b phase-{N}-{short-description}
```

**Branch naming:**

- `phase-{N}-{description}` ? implementation phases
- `fix-{issue}` ? bug fixes
- `docs-{topic}` ? documentation updates
- `chore/{topic}` ? tooling/workflow (e.g. `chore/auto-orchestration-workflow`)

### 2. Implementation

Orchestrator delegates to generalPurpose with:

- `spec.md` phase scope
- `.cursor/skills/langgraph-bug-triage/SKILL.md`

Commit incrementally:

```
[verb] [what] [(optional context)]

Examples:
- Add preprocess node with text cleaning
- Implement two-stage duplicate detection
- Fix ValidationError handling in triage node
```

### 3. Spec Review (conditional)

If `git diff main -- spec.md` is non-empty ? `@spec-architect`. Otherwise skip.

### 4. Code Audit (mandatory)

`@code-auditor` audits against `spec.md`. Critical issues ? `@bug-fixer` ? re-audit (max 2 loops).

### 5. QA Test (mandatory)

| Phase | QA scope |
|-------|----------|
| 1 | Environment validation only |
| 2+ | Full Set B + edge cases |

Failures ? `@bug-fixer` ? re-test (max 3 loops).

### 6. Push Branch

```bash
git push -u origin phase-{N}-{description}
```

### 7. Create PR

```bash
gh pr create \
  --title "Phase {N}: {Title}" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
[What this phase implements]

## Changes
- [Change 1]
- [Change 2]

## Agent-Generated vs Manual
**Agent generated:**
- [Files/code generated by AI]

**Manually changed:**
- [Files you modified after agent]

## Audit Result
- **Code auditor:** [pass | warnings | critical]

## QA Results
- **Mode:** [environment-only | full Set B]
- **Score:** [X/Y passed]

## Testing
- [ ] Phase-appropriate checks

## Addresses
- Spec requirement: [from spec.md]
- Exercise requirement: [from 1_candidate_brief.md]
EOF
)"
```

### 8. Review & Merge (user-initiated)

Orchestrator reports PR URL. User says `merge` when ready:

```bash
gh pr merge {number} --squash
```

