## Exercise Requirement Compliance

The brief states:

> "Commit your work to the Gitea repo and open at least one PR ? we want to see the flow end to end"

**Our approach:**

1. Each phase = 1 PR
2. Orchestrator runs audit + QA before every PR
3. PR description documents agent vs manual work
4. User merges when satisfied

---

## Git Best Practices

### DO:

- Use phase-orchestrator for every phase
- Create feature branch for each phase
- Commit logical units of work
- Document agent-generated vs manual in PR
- Run audit + QA before PR (orchestrator enforces)

### DON'T:

- Work directly on main for implementation
- Ask user which agent to invoke mid-pipeline
- Skip code-auditor or qa-tester
- Merge without user saying "merge"
- Force-push main

